  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "The most likely cause of the flaw growth is original fabrication associated with the nozzle to safe end replacements of 1982/1983. This nozzle to safe end weld, at the 3 o'clock position required multiple defect repairs including flapping, grinding and localized welding at the Inconel Alloy 182/82 nozzle cladding and root pass. These local repairs cause residual stresses internal to the weld that can create sites for Stress Corrosion Cracking (SCC). For this weld the original susceptible Inconel Alloy 182 nozzle butter material creates a region where the risk of crack initiation is increased.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "Original fabrication defects/repairs induced residual stresses enabling IGSCC in susceptible Inconel 182 weld material",
    "provisional": true
  },
